2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - - Standardized tests (SAT/ACT) provide a common metric across different schools and contexts, which can help identify talented students from under-resourced high schools
2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - - They have decent predictive validity for first-year college GPA
2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - - They can reduce advantage from grade inflation or variable grading standards
2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - **Where your friend's position has merit:**
2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - - Standardized tests correlate heavily with family income and parental education—they measure test-taking ability and preparation access, not just aptitude
2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - - Wealthy students can afford expensive prep courses; this advantages the already-privileged
2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - - Multiple studies show test scores predict college success only modestly better than high school GPA alone
2026-05-09 17:58:10,380 - INFO - - They may discourage qualified low-income students from applying (stereotype threat is real, though debated)
