2026-05-09 17:58:35,641 - INFO - **Where you're likely right:**
2026-05-09 17:58:35,641 - INFO - - Companies systematically collect *far more* data than necessary for service improvement, then use it for surveillance, manipulation, and sale to third parties
2026-05-09 17:58:35,641 - INFO - - "Improving services" is often pretext; the real driver is ad targeting and behavioral prediction
2026-05-09 17:58:35,641 - INFO - - Market competition doesn't constrain this—users can't realistically opt out, and they don't see what's happening
2026-05-09 17:58:35,642 - INFO - - Real harms are documented: discrimination, manipulation, privacy violations, security breaches
2026-05-09 17:58:35,642 - INFO - 
